2. Collectors — INTERNALS (Interview Favorite)
🔹 What is a Collector?

A Collector defines:

How to create a container

How to add elements

How to merge partial results

How to finish result

Collector has 4 core parts:
supplier()     // create container
accumulator()  // add element
combiner()     // merge (parallel)
finisher()     // final transform

Example: Collectors.toList()

Internally:

supplier()    -> new ArrayList<>()
accumulator() -> list.add(element)
combiner()    -> list1.addAll(list2)
finisher()    -> identity

🔥 groupingBy() Deep Internals
Collectors.groupingBy(
    classifier,      // Function<T, K>
    mapFactory,      // Supplier<Map>
    downstream       // Collector
)


Your example:

Function.identity()      // key logic
LinkedHashMap::new       // preserve order
Collectors.counting()   // downstream collector

🎯 Interview Line

“Collectors encapsulate mutable reduction logic and handle parallel merging safely.”
